WEBVTT

00:00:00.332 --> 00:00:01.281
Grid Bot Builder.

00:00:01.819 --> 00:00:02.880
Grid Bot Blueprint.

00:00:03.340 --> 00:00:04.074
Lesson one.

00:00:04.626 --> 00:00:05.355
Introduction.

00:00:06.470 --> 00:00:07.616
Education only.

00:00:08.175 --> 00:00:09.489
Not financial advice.

00:00:10.009 --> 00:00:12.061
This is general information and

00:00:12.061 --> 00:00:14.264
doesn't consider your objectives,

00:00:14.264 --> 00:00:16.164
financial situation or needs.

00:00:16.684 --> 00:00:18.002
Crypto is high risk.

00:00:18.522 --> 00:00:20.757
You could lose all the money you put in.

00:00:21.467 --> 00:00:23.583
Crypto carries a risk of total loss.

00:00:24.783 --> 00:00:26.839
The prices are public historical

00:00:26.839 --> 00:00:28.601
daily closes, marked Example.

00:00:29.121 --> 00:00:31.188
A close is the last price of the day.

00:00:32.343 --> 00:00:34.408
Past performance is not a reliable

00:00:34.408 --> 00:00:36.117
indicator of future results.

00:00:37.317 --> 00:00:39.682
A grid bot places waiting buy orders

00:00:39.682 --> 00:00:41.810
on lines below the price and sell

00:00:41.810 --> 00:00:43.939
orders on lines above it, inside a

00:00:43.939 --> 00:00:45.673
top and a bottom you choose.

00:00:46.193 --> 00:00:47.869
The space between your top and

00:00:47.869 --> 00:00:49.600
your bottom is called the band.

00:00:50.390 --> 00:00:52.096
A limit order is an order that

00:00:52.096 --> 00:00:53.660
waits at a price you choose.

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:55.744
It does not chase the price.

00:00:56.163 --> 00:00:57.727
Chasing the price would mean

00:00:57.727 --> 00:00:59.180
moving the order to follow

00:00:59.180 --> 00:01:00.744
wherever the price has gone.

00:01:01.743 --> 00:01:03.923
The sells above need some coin, so a

00:01:03.923 --> 00:01:06.180
grid starts with part cash and part

00:01:06.180 --> 00:01:08.359
coin, and that is a description, not

00:01:08.359 --> 00:01:09.994
advice about what to hold.

00:01:10.514 --> 00:01:12.078
Cash is money you can spend.

00:01:12.676 --> 00:01:13.738
Coin is the crypto.

00:01:14.829 --> 00:01:16.561
A stop is a rule you write down

00:01:16.561 --> 00:01:18.245
before you start, saying what

00:01:18.245 --> 00:01:20.024
you will do if the price leaves

00:01:20.024 --> 00:01:21.812
the band and does not come back.

00:01:23.004 --> 00:01:24.850
When a chart says Example, it

00:01:24.850 --> 00:01:26.696
means a real past price used

00:01:26.696 --> 00:01:28.541
as an example, not a forecast.

00:01:29.741 --> 00:01:31.082
By the end you will know

00:01:31.082 --> 00:01:32.367
what a grid bot places.

00:01:33.496 --> 00:01:35.575
You will see that idea on

00:01:35.575 --> 00:01:37.550
one real path from 2023.

00:01:38.750 --> 00:01:40.258
You will be able to say the

00:01:40.258 --> 00:01:41.711
stop rule in one sentence.

00:01:42.665 --> 00:01:44.620
Think of a ladder leaned on a wall.

00:01:44.762 --> 00:01:47.108
The rungs wait, and they do not chase you.

00:01:47.384 --> 00:01:49.428
The ladder is the analogy, and the

00:01:49.428 --> 00:01:51.700
chart beside it is the real past path.

00:01:52.750 --> 00:01:54.593
The range is the top line and the

00:01:54.593 --> 00:01:56.437
bottom line, taken from the path.

00:01:56.916 --> 00:01:58.368
Every close in this window

00:01:58.368 --> 00:02:00.100
stayed between those two lines.

00:02:00.886 --> 00:02:02.725
The range is a top and a bottom

00:02:02.725 --> 00:02:04.258
you draw before any rung.

00:02:04.778 --> 00:02:06.287
Without a top and a bottom,

00:02:06.287 --> 00:02:07.739
you can't place the lines.

00:02:08.801 --> 00:02:11.393
Six equal gaps of about 900 dollars sit

00:02:11.393 --> 00:02:14.066
between the bottom line and the top line.

00:02:14.586 --> 00:02:16.813
Each gap is about 900 dollars:

00:02:16.813 --> 00:02:19.040
the top line minus the bottom

00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:20.525
line, divided by six.

00:02:21.045 --> 00:02:22.380
It is one step between

00:02:22.380 --> 00:02:23.863
lines, not the whole band.

00:02:24.383 --> 00:02:26.222
Seven lines make those six gaps.

00:02:26.742 --> 00:02:28.473
A limit order waits on a level.

00:02:28.830 --> 00:02:30.617
It does not run after the price.

00:02:31.541 --> 00:02:33.049
The levels are limit orders

00:02:33.049 --> 00:02:34.334
that wait on the rungs.

00:02:34.652 --> 00:02:36.328
A limit order sits at a price.

00:02:36.830 --> 00:02:37.864
It does not chase.

00:02:39.064 --> 00:02:41.392
A fence has a top rail and a bottom rail.

00:02:41.912 --> 00:02:43.863
Inside them, the price can wander.

00:02:44.383 --> 00:02:46.205
On the chart those rails are the

00:02:46.205 --> 00:02:47.825
bottom line and the top line.

00:02:48.867 --> 00:02:50.096
The daily close is the

00:02:50.096 --> 00:02:51.325
last price of the day.

00:02:51.746 --> 00:02:53.546
Crypto trades all day, so the

00:02:53.546 --> 00:02:54.954
day is cut at a set time.

00:02:55.474 --> 00:02:57.458
This is a simple candle that shows

00:02:57.458 --> 00:02:59.134
the day's high, low and close.

00:02:59.608 --> 00:03:01.537
Traders call it a candle because

00:03:01.537 --> 00:03:03.466
the full version has a thick body

00:03:03.466 --> 00:03:05.198
and a thin wick, like a candle.

00:03:05.630 --> 00:03:07.138
Here we only need the high,

00:03:07.138 --> 00:03:08.367
the low and the close.

00:03:08.701 --> 00:03:11.881
This candle is 19 July 2023.

00:03:12.401 --> 00:03:13.630
The high, the low, and

00:03:13.630 --> 00:03:14.915
the close are labelled.

00:03:15.807 --> 00:03:17.937
The example is Bitcoin's public

00:03:17.937 --> 00:03:19.593
daily price in US dollars.

00:03:20.113 --> 00:03:23.311
From 19 July 2023 to 16 October

00:03:23.311 --> 00:03:26.254
2023, every one of those days

00:03:26.254 --> 00:03:28.686
closed inside the band.

00:03:29.206 --> 00:03:30.993
We do not need to read each day.

00:03:31.259 --> 00:03:32.602
The shape is the lesson,

00:03:32.602 --> 00:03:34.016
and it is marked Example.

00:03:35.066 --> 00:03:36.798
A stop is a rule you write down

00:03:36.798 --> 00:03:38.482
before you start, saying what

00:03:38.482 --> 00:03:40.261
you will do if the price leaves

00:03:40.261 --> 00:03:42.049
the band and does not come back.

00:03:42.561 --> 00:03:44.989
On 23 October 2023 the close

00:03:44.989 --> 00:03:47.417
finished above the top line.

00:03:47.937 --> 00:03:49.502
The price did not come back,

00:03:49.502 --> 00:03:51.122
so this example was finished.

00:03:51.928 --> 00:03:53.045
Write your stop rule

00:03:53.045 --> 00:03:54.274
down before you start.

00:03:54.570 --> 00:03:57.191
On the card it says: Stop = when you quit.

00:03:58.391 --> 00:04:01.147
Worked check: 19 July

00:04:01.147 --> 00:04:04.227
2023 to 16 October 2023.

00:04:04.747 --> 00:04:07.420
Six equal gaps of about 900 dollars.

00:04:07.940 --> 00:04:09.448
The low is the bottom line.

00:04:09.928 --> 00:04:11.394
The high is the top line.

00:04:12.444 --> 00:04:14.526
The stop rule is: if the daily close

00:04:14.526 --> 00:04:16.458
leaves the top line and does not

00:04:16.458 --> 00:04:18.316
come back, the idea is finished.

00:04:18.836 --> 00:04:20.680
Nothing on this card is an order.

00:04:21.643 --> 00:04:23.254
Price often moves sideways,

00:04:23.254 --> 00:04:25.004
bouncing between the same top

00:04:25.004 --> 00:04:26.754
and bottom instead of leaving.

00:04:27.274 --> 00:04:28.852
A grid is a ladder of limit

00:04:28.852 --> 00:04:30.806
orders built for that bouncing.

00:04:31.326 --> 00:04:33.182
When price runs one way and stays

00:04:33.182 --> 00:04:35.304
there, the bot has nothing left to do.

00:04:36.375 --> 00:04:38.415
A grid has three parts you can name:

00:04:38.415 --> 00:04:40.427
the range, the levels, and the stop.

00:04:40.903 --> 00:04:42.132
The range is the band.

00:04:42.643 --> 00:04:44.598
The levels are the rungs inside it.

00:04:45.647 --> 00:04:48.062
Buy orders sit on lines below the price

00:04:48.062 --> 00:04:50.325
and sell orders sit on lines above it.

00:04:50.845 --> 00:04:52.921
An order fills when the price reaches

00:04:52.921 --> 00:04:54.652
its line and the trade happens.

00:04:55.114 --> 00:04:57.253
The sells need some coin, so a grid

00:04:57.253 --> 00:04:59.550
starts with part cash and part coin,

00:04:59.550 --> 00:05:01.926
and that is a description, not advice.

00:05:03.126 --> 00:05:05.026
No order is sent from this lesson.

00:05:05.356 --> 00:05:06.366
You draw the idea.

00:05:06.886 --> 00:05:08.680
If a screen appears later, it

00:05:08.680 --> 00:05:10.395
should be a copy of the page,

00:05:10.395 --> 00:05:11.955
and only on paper or demo.

00:05:13.155 --> 00:05:14.775
The course is a map, and this

00:05:14.775 --> 00:05:16.898
introduction is only the first square.

00:05:17.493 --> 00:05:18.637
Next is a checklist.

00:05:19.658 --> 00:05:20.775
Then the definition.

00:05:21.123 --> 00:05:22.825
Then calm or trending markets.

00:05:23.525 --> 00:05:24.862
Then spacing and range.

00:05:25.562 --> 00:05:26.928
Then entry and exit.

00:05:27.686 --> 00:05:28.804
Then a paper screen.

00:05:29.721 --> 00:05:30.615
Then monitoring.

00:05:31.136 --> 00:05:31.994
Then mistakes.

00:05:32.737 --> 00:05:33.562
Then scaling.

00:05:34.262 --> 00:05:36.387
Then an opt-in lesson on liquidation.

00:05:37.437 --> 00:05:39.280
A fill is that trade at the line.

00:05:39.668 --> 00:05:42.067
As price climbs, each sell order fills.

00:05:42.267 --> 00:05:43.799
So you end up holding cash.

00:05:44.319 --> 00:05:46.723
As price falls, each buy order fills.

00:05:46.923 --> 00:05:48.432
So you end up holding coin.

00:05:50.575 --> 00:05:52.866
There is no result number in this lesson.

00:05:53.002 --> 00:05:54.622
A result number would pretend

00:05:54.622 --> 00:05:56.242
the example already happened.

00:05:56.555 --> 00:05:58.992
The example is a drawing of a mechanism.

00:06:00.192 --> 00:06:02.358
The next step is the setup checklist,

00:06:02.358 --> 00:06:03.946
on paper, before any screen.

00:06:04.466 --> 00:06:06.366
You will need the three words when

00:06:06.366 --> 00:06:08.321
that checklist asks what a grid is.

00:06:09.001 --> 00:06:10.689
A paper or demo account is

00:06:10.689 --> 00:06:12.296
a fence around practice.

00:06:12.816 --> 00:06:14.157
Inside the fence you can

00:06:14.157 --> 00:06:15.442
see fields and buttons.

00:06:15.815 --> 00:06:17.156
You still do not send an

00:06:17.156 --> 00:06:18.329
order in this course.

00:06:19.122 --> 00:06:20.701
If you keep one sentence,

00:06:20.701 --> 00:06:22.438
keep this: range, levels, and

00:06:22.438 --> 00:06:24.253
stop, drawn before any click.

00:06:24.773 --> 00:06:26.416
Bouncing inside the band is

00:06:26.416 --> 00:06:27.813
what a grid is built for.

00:06:28.293 --> 00:06:29.531
The exit from the band

00:06:29.531 --> 00:06:30.837
is the failure picture.

00:06:32.037 --> 00:06:34.196
A grid bot places waiting buys below

00:06:34.196 --> 00:06:36.355
the price and waiting sells above it.

00:06:37.555 --> 00:06:40.036
This 2023 path stayed between the

00:06:40.036 --> 00:06:42.695
bottom line and the top line, with six

00:06:42.695 --> 00:06:45.265
gaps of about 900 between the lines.

00:06:46.465 --> 00:06:48.588
The stop rule says what you will do if

00:06:48.588 --> 00:06:50.823
the price leaves and does not come back.

00:06:51.632 --> 00:06:53.867
Next lesson: What you are going to need.

00:06:54.256 --> 00:06:56.024
The pair is the two things you

00:06:56.024 --> 00:06:58.013
swap, like Bitcoin and US dollars.

00:06:58.533 --> 00:07:00.978
Bring a notebook, the top and bottom

00:07:00.978 --> 00:07:03.171
of the band, the gaps between the

00:07:03.171 --> 00:07:05.194
lines, paper or demo, your stop

00:07:05.194 --> 00:07:07.049
rule, and no secrets: no seed

00:07:07.049 --> 00:07:09.326
phrase, private key or API secret.

00:07:09.846 --> 00:07:11.868
Leave every figure marked EXAMPLE,

00:07:11.868 --> 00:07:13.960
and no order is sent between lessons.

